          "content": "<p>The club is aware that supporters may currently be encountering issues accessing their tickets for tomorrow&rsquo;s Sky Bet League One fixture against Reading due to the global Microsoft outage.</p>\n<p>If the outage continues into Saturday, supporters unable to download their tickets will need to bring their supporter ID and a form of personal identification with them to the ticket office at Edgeley Park, so our team can verify your booking and provide you with a physical ticket for the game.</p>\n<p>Due to this issue, we advise that all supporters arrive at Edgeley Park an hour ahead of kick-off to avoid significant queuing time.</p>\n<p>Your supporter ID number can be found in the bottom left corner when logging in to your <a href=\"https://tickets.stockportcounty.com/\">online ticketing account.</a></p>\n<p>If you purchased your ticket using a Microsoft Outlook email address and can still access it, we recommend downloading it to your digital wallet ahead of the game.</p>\n<p>We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide further updates as soon as more information becomes available.</p>",
